         "Here we introduce JAX, M.D. which is a new MD package that leverages the substantial progress made in ML software to improve this state of affairs. JAX, M.D. is end-to-end differentiable, written in pure python, and is written in JAX which has a strong neural network ecosystem that can be used seamlessly with simulations. In addition to AD, JAX provides a number of features that are well-suited for physics simulations. In particular, code can be just-in-time compiled to XLA which allows simulations written in JAX, M.D. to run efficiently on CPU, GPU, or TPU with no changes to the code. Finally, JAX provides tools to automatically vectorize calculations over one- or multiple-devices that allows JAX, M.D. to easily simulate ensembles of systems.\n",
